 ## Overview
-Sparse Volume Texture Setup is a method for importing and configuring large, sparse volumetric datasets (up to ~6 gigavoxels) into Unreal Engine 5 using Sparse Volume Textures (SVT) [S1, S2, unofficial][S3]. It solves the problem of rendering massive volumetric data without chunking artifacts by storing data in sparse tiles within a single large volume texture, thereby circumventing the DirectX 12 API limit of 2048 voxels per dimension [S2, unofficial][S3]. Unlike debug viewers or fog-specific renderers, it supports full lighting, emission, and color, making it suitable for scientific data visualization [S1, unofficial]. It builds on [Volume Texture Setup](4055-volume-texture-setup.md) by defining the specific material and actor workflow required to visualize the data [S3].
